{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZbws8DZXV7AaCRszxLG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n1. Controllers use Spring annotations: `@PostMapping`, `@GetMapping`, `@PathVariable`\n2. Status codes: 201 (CREATED) via `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED)`, direct object return for GET\n3. Error handling via sealed `ApiException` subclasses: `ConflictException` (409), `ResourceNotFoundException` (404)\n4. `GlobalExceptionHandler` converts exceptions to `ApiError` response envelope\n5. Tests use `MockMvc`, `status()`, and `jsonPath()` assertions\n6. Tests reset repository state in `@BeforeEach`\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Add error code for CANCELLED shipment conflict (cannot avoid, new error case)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add confirm endpoint (core requirement)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for confirm endpoint cases (required by ticket acceptance)\n\n**Risks:**\n\n1. Breaking existing tests if endpoint signature is wrong\n2. Missing the idempotent case (CONFIRMED stays CONFIRMED)\n3. Not persisting the state change to the repository\n4. Using wrong HTTP status codes (should be 409 for CANCELLED, 404 for missing, 200 for success)\n5. Not using the error handling pattern established by other endpoints\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket clearly specifies the transitions and status codes.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to handle attempts to confirm CANCELLED shipments (409).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if missing)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM`\n   - If status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED and persist via repository\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - Return the shipment with HTTP 200\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test cases:\n   - Confirm a CREATED shipment → moves to CONFIRMED, returns the shipment\n   - Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment → succeeds, no change\n   - Confirm a CANCELLED shipment → 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n   - Confirm a non-existent shipment → 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected:** Instead of modifying Shipment (immutable data class), I could create a new Shipment object with updated status and save it. This is better than mutating the object or creating a separate persistence method. The repository's `save` method handles both insert and update via ConcurrentHashMap.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED)**: Read shipment, check status is CREATED, create new Shipment with CONFIRMED status, save via repository, return 200 with updated shipment\n- **Idempotent case (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED)**: Read shipment, check status is CONFIRMED, save (no-op via same key), return 200 with unchanged shipment\n- **Error case (CANCELLED)**: Read shipment, throw ConflictException → handled by GlobalExceptionHandler → 409 with ApiError body\n- **Error case (not found)**: Throw ResourceNotFoundException → handled by GlobalExceptionHandler → 404 with ApiError body\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n2. Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change\n3. Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n4. Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":16357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":678},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19af8de3-810d-42a8-a57e-77e22c95d588","uuid":"feb72a64-d2c6-4905-a12a-8239820ded35","timestamp":"2026-09-30T12:12:57.232Z","request_id":"req_011CfZbwrkQHRMxtcxnkYB31"}
